# Opensource UI — Component Design

Apply when creating or editing files under `components/`. Each file must be **copy-paste ready** — a user copies one file (+ `cn`, icons) into their Next.js app without providers or theme config.

Design authority: `skills/opensource-ui/references/design.md`.

## Visual language

### Colors (Tailwind)

| Role | Token | Usage |
| ---- | ----- | ----- |
| Ink | `neutral-900` | Primary text, focus borders |
| Ink soft | `neutral-800` | Primary button fill |
| Body | `neutral-700` | Muted paragraphs |
| Muted | `neutral-500` | Meta, secondary nav |
| Faint | `neutral-400` | Placeholders, hints |
| Paper | `white` | Card and field backgrounds |
| Paper tint | `neutral-50` | Disabled / recessed fills |
| Border | `neutral-200` | Default input borders |
| Border subtle | `neutral-100` | Hairline card edges |
| Rose | `rose-500` | Errors, required `*` |
| Cyan | `cyan-200` | Rare demo accents only |

**Banned:** `purple-*`, `violet-*`, `indigo-*` anywhere.

### Typography

- **UI controls** (buttons, inputs, labels, nav): Geist sans — default body classes
- **Never** put Instrument Serif on dense controls
- **Never** introduce Inter, Plus Jakarta, DM Sans, or other default AI fonts

### Shape and spacing

- Buttons: `rounded-md` (6px), `px-4 py-2`
- Fields and small cards: `rounded-lg` (8px), `h-10` for inputs
- Editorial / testimonial surfaces: `rounded-2xl` (16px)
- Internal padding: `p-4` typical
- Flat surfaces — no ambient card shadows; no gradients or glow

### Inputs and focus

```tsx
// ✅ Opensource UI input focus
className="border border-neutral-200 bg-white outline-none ring-0 focus:border-neutral-900 focus:ring-0"

// ❌ Never
className="focus:ring-2 focus:ring-sky-500"
```

Errors: `border-rose-500` + visible error text. Required fields: rose asterisk.

## File structure and imports

**Allowed external imports only:**

- `cn` from `@/lib/cn`
- `Link` from `next/link`
- `Image` from `next/image` (when the component uses images)
- Icons from `lucide-react` and/or `@/icons/...`

Everything else — types, hooks, helpers, sub-components — lives **in the same file**.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
import Link from "next/link";
import { Mail } from "lucide-react";
import { Github } from "@/icons/brands/github";
import { cn } from "@/lib/cn";

// ❌ BAD — shared hook, barrel, or raw anchor
import { useOtpField } from "./use-otp-input";
<a href="/login">Sign in</a>
```

### Navigation links

- Use **`Link`** for real routes
- Use **`<button type="button">`** styled as a link for `#` or empty demo hrefs

## Component API

- Interactive elements: **`forwardRef`**
- Props: extend native HTML element types (`ComponentPropsWithoutRef<"button">`, etc.)
- Classes: merge with **`cn()`**
- **`"use client"`** only when needed (state, effects, events, browser APIs)
- Export named component matching filename (`login-form.tsx` → `LoginForm`)
- Ship **real demo content** — names, numbers, labels that look like real UI, not gray placeholders

## Production quality

- Pass ESLint with no errors or warnings
- Handle disabled, error, controlled/uncontrolled, keyboard, and a11y labels
- Match conventions in sibling files in the same category folder
- **Tailwind v4 utilities only** — no `<style>`, no `@keyframes` in component files, no inline `style={{}}`, no new rules in `globals.css` for component styling

## Category folders

Organize by purpose: `buttons/`, `inputs/`, `forms/`, `widgets/`, `mockups/`, `notifications/`, `table/`, `travel/`, `socials/`, etc. Folder name drives docs category in the showcase (e.g. `widgets/` → **Widgets**).

After adding a component, register it in `lib/showcase/showcase.tsx` — see `showcase-registry.mdc`.
